-- title:
--   Regular prolongation of A extending a given discrete valuation
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and $M'\neq 0$, and write $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and $F=$ `fieldBar q M'` for the full-level function field, an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ inside the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, and put $A_0=A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$). Assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, and that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c\in k_0\cap A$. Give $F$ the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\subseteq F$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F_0=F$ (the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is $\top$), and every valuation subring $W$ of $F_0$ such that $W\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$ (an element of $k_0$ lies in $A$ iff its image lies in $W$), $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, and the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by the image of $\pi_0$, there exist a field $FI$ with an algebra structure over the residue field of $A$ and a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ to $F$ with reduced field $FI$ — that is, a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ together with a surjective ring homomorphism $R.\mathrm{residue}$ to $FI$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$, satisfying $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,x\in R.\mathrm{integers}\iff x\in A$ for $x\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, compatibility of $R.\mathrm{residue}$ with the residue map of $A$, and the condition that every nonzero $f\in F$ has a scalar $c\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $c\cdot f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ of nonzero residue — such that $R.\mathrm{integers}\cap F_0=W$ (for $f\in F_0$, $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}\iff f\in W$) and every element of $FI$ is the $R$-residue of some element of $F_0$ lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$.
--
--   This is the local lifting step that extends a valuation of the constant field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, together with a prescribed discrete valuation $W$ of a model field $F_0$ over which the full-level function field is generated by constants, to a regular prolongation with the same reduced field; the hypotheses on $A\cap k_0$ make all finite layers of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ totally ramified, so the prolongation can be built along the tower. It is invoked in the construction of Igusa branches and of the component charts of the semistable model at full level, for instance by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_branchPlace_igusaEnd_integral_overS_of_node_crossingPresentation_igusaBranch`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_branchPlace_igusaEnd_integral_overS_of_node_crossingPresentation_igusaBranch) and in the descent statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent).
